    "prompt": "Cinematic moody film, 16:9, cold desaturated teal-gray grade, crushed blacks, subtle film grain, heavy storm-overcast sky, violent North Atlantic ocean, giant white waves exploding against towering black basalt sea cliffs (Faroe Islands style), strong wind throughout. \n\nCharacters: the woman from @image1 — keep her exact face, hairstyle and full outfit; the man from @image2 — keep his exact face, hairstyle and full outfit. \n\nShot 1 (0–3s): Extreme wide establishing shot, camera locked-off with a barely perceptible slow push-in: a massive wave detonates against the dark cliffs; on a low flat rocky promontory at the water's edge, the tiny figures of the couple stand facing each other, dwarfed by the ocean and spray. \n\nShot 2 (3–6s): Cut to a windswept handheld medium shot on the promontory: the woman (@image1) reaches out, the man (@image2) takes her hand and pulls her in, lifting her off the ground into a spinning embrace; she wraps around him laughing, her long hair whipping across the frame; the camera slowly orbits the couple, stormy sea churning behind them. \n\nShot 3 (6–9s): Medium-full shot at the very edge of the wet rock: they kiss as waves burst into spray on the stones below; then cut to an extreme close-up of the kiss, softer diffused light, shallow depth of field, wind-blown strands of hair crossing the lens. \n\nShot 4 (9–11s): Extreme close-up, side profile: their foreheads nearly touching, her eyes glassy and hurt, his expression suddenly cold and distant; the romance turns into tension; wind tears at her hair. \n\nShot 5 (0:12-0:14s) - The Push. - HARD CUT to a MEDIUM WIDE SIDE SHOT. - The SAME woman from @image1 and the SAME man from @image2 are now visible standing close to the edge of the SAME volcanic cliff. - Preserve their exact identities and clothing. - Maintain geographical continuity with all previous shots. ACTION: - For a brief moment, they remain standing extremely close together. - Then the emotional tone suddenly changes. - The man from - @image1 places both hands against the woman's upper arms / shoulders. - He gives the woman ONE sudden firm push backward. - The push happens only once. The push is brief, sudden and physically realistic. - No exaggerated superhero force. - The woman from @image2 is visibly surprised and immediately loses her balance. - She takes several unstable backward steps toward the edge of the cliff. - Her arms instinctively move outward as she tries to regain her balance. - Her facial expression naturally changes to shock and confusion. - Strong wind dramatically moves her hair and clothing. - Her body movement must follow realistic momentum, balance and gravity. \n\nShot 6 (14–18s): SLOW CINEMATIC FALL - HARD CUT TO A COMPLETELY NEW CAMERA ANGLE. - Dramatic high overhead aerial camera angle looking downward beside the enormous vertical black cliff. - The woman from @image1 is already falling backward through open air. - The man is NOT falling. The man remains above on the cliff and does not need to be visible in this shot. - TIME FEELS DRAMATICALLY SLOWED DOWN. - The woman's fall is intentionally slow, dramatic and cinematic. \n\nTHE WOMAN: - At the beginning of this shot, the camera is relatively close above the falling woman. - We see the front of her body and her face as she falls backward. - Her face is clearly visible looking upward toward the camera. - HER FACE MUST REMAIN EXACTLY RECOGNIZABLE AS @image1. - Do NOT change her facial identity because of the unusual camera angle. - Her expression is shocked and breathless: eyes wide, mouth slightly open, natural fear, confusion and surprise. - No exaggerated screaming expression. - Her arms slowly spread outward as she falls. - Her legs react naturally to the loss of support. - Her hair streams dramatically upward relative to her falling body because of downward motion, gravity and strong airflow. - Her clothing from @image1 reacts naturally to the airflow but remains exactly the same clothing. - The fabric moves upward and backward naturally due to the fall and wind. - Correct realistic clothing physics, hair physics, gravity and human anatomy. \n\nCAMERA: - The camera follows her downward but moves slightly SLOWER than her falling body. - Therefore, the distance between the camera and the woman gradually increases. - At first she is relatively large in the frame. - Then she becomes progressively smaller. And smaller. And smaller. - The camera gradually reveals the enormous vertical black cliff surrounding her. - The scale becomes increasingly dramatic. \n\nENVIRONMENT: - Far beneath her, the dark turbulent ocean becomes visible. - White sea foam swirls around the base of the enormous cliff. - Natural waves crash against the rocks far below. - The woman gradually becomes a small human figure surrounded by the gigantic cliff and ocean. - Emphasize the enormous height and scale of the environment. - The final composition should make the woman look increasingly tiny compared with the gigantic landscape. \n\nENDING: - DO NOT show her reaching the water. - DO NOT show impact. - DO NOT show injury. - DO NOT show blood. - END THE VIDEO WHILE THE WOMAN FROM @image1 IS STILL FALLING THROUGH OPEN AIR. - The final frame should feel suspended, dramatic and unresolved. CINEMATIC STYLE - High-end live-action cinema. Ultra photorealistic. - Realistic human skin, natural skin texture, natural facial micro-expressions. - Realistic anatomy, realistic human body weight, realistic physical interactions between the characters. - Realistic wind physics, hair physics, fabric physics, gravity, ocean physics. - Cold desaturated cinematic color grading, dark blue-grey tones. - Natural cloudy daylight, dramatic overcast atmosphere. - Subtle realistic film grain, natural cinematic motion blur. - Atmospheric depth, realistic lens behavior. - No artificial CGI appearance."
