    "prompt": "Create a 15-second cinematic surreal photorealistic video.\n\n@image1 is the main character. Use the exact appearance, clothing, face, body shape, hairstyle, and identity from @image1. Do not redesign the character. Do not change gender, age, outfit, hairstyle, face, or body proportions.\n\nThe scene takes place in a natural surreal world with no concrete buildings. The environment is a huge meadow of tall grass and giant plants. Far in the background, if visible, homes are built naturally inside enormous tree trunks and tree crowns, like organic tree-houses. No modern city, no stone buildings, no concrete architecture.\n\nMAIN CONCEPT:\nA giant dandelion is used as a natural flying transport station. The dandelion must be enormous, the size of a giant tree, at least 20-30 meters tall, much taller than the character. It is not a small flower and not a normal dandelion. The thick green stem is like a tree trunk. At the top is a large walkable central seed head / receptacle platform, wide enough for the character to physically stand and walk on.\n\nVERY IMPORTANT STRUCTURE:\nThe dandelion must already have many separate visible basket-seeds before the wind blows.\nThere must be about 24 to 36 large, clearly separated dandelion seed units arranged around the giant seed head.\nEach seed unit is separate and easy to see:\none long thin stem/filament grows out from the central dandelion head,\nat the end of that filament is one large white fluffy dandelion parachute,\nand directly under that same parachute hangs one small woven basket.\nSo each seed has its own basket.\nThese baskets are not hidden and must be visible before the takeoff.\nDo not create only one basket.\nDo not place one single basket under the entire dandelion like a hot-air balloon.\nDo not make a dense cloud of tiny seeds.\nThe seed-baskets must be spaced far apart, with visible air gaps between them, so the structure is readable and not crowded.\n\nCONTINUITY RULE:\nThe number of baskets must stay consistent through the whole video.\nIf the dandelion starts with about 24-36 visible basket-seeds, then only those same basket-seeds fly away.\nNo new baskets may appear after the wind.\nNo extra passengers or baskets may suddenly appear in the sky.\nMost baskets are empty. A few distant baskets may contain small background people in normal everyday clothing, but they must be visible already before the wind and remain background only.\nThe main focus is always the character from @image1.\n\nSHOT BREAKDOWN:\n\n0-3 seconds:\nMedium cinematic shot on top of the giant dandelion head. The character @image1 walks on the broad central seed-head platform. The scale should feel huge: the platform is like a natural rooftop made of dandelion texture. Around the character, we can already see several large separate seed-baskets attached around the edge of the platform. The character approaches one specific woven basket attached to one seed unit and climbs inside it, holding the basket rim. Keep the camera close enough for emotion, but make sure more than one basket is already visible in the background or around the edge.\n\n3-6 seconds:\nThe camera pulls back and rises in one smooth epic move, revealing the full structure. We now clearly see the whole giant dandelion: a tree-sized thick green stem, a broad central seed-head platform at the top, and around it 24-36 large separate dandelion seed parachutes, each with its own woven basket hanging underneath. The seed-baskets are arranged in a wide, open, radial formation, not tightly packed. Most baskets are empty and gently swaying. A few background people may be visible in distant baskets, but small and secondary. The dandelion should look enormous, like a tree or natural tower in a meadow of tall grass.\n\n6-8 seconds:\nA strong gust of wind arrives. Tall grass bends in waves. The 24-36 visible seed-baskets begin to tremble and lift. They detach from the central dandelion head in a physically continuous way. The exact same visible seed-baskets that were attached a moment ago are the ones that fly away. No new baskets appear. The central platform remains behind as the seed-baskets pull free and scatter outward.\n\n8-11 seconds:\nThe camera follows the specific seed-basket carrying @image1. It flies on the wind like a giant dandelion seed parachute with a woven basket underneath. The fluffy white parachute above the basket bends and vibrates in the airflow. The character holds the rim as wind pushes clothing and hair. Other seed-baskets pass through the background, but only the same limited number from the original dandelion. Do not fill the sky with hundreds of new baskets.\n\n11-15 seconds:\nClose-to-wide cinematic flight shot. The character looks around with wonder and joy, enjoying the surreal flight. The basket moves fast but gracefully through golden-hour light. The camera pulls back to a beautiful wide final shot: the character's basket flying among a limited group of the original dandelion basket-seeds, all spread naturally through the air with lots of space between them. The world below is a vast natural meadow with huge grass and tree-homes in the distance. End mid-flight in warm cinematic sunlight. No landing.\n\nVISUAL STYLE:\nExtreme cinematic realism, Hollywood-level camera and lighting. Photorealistic textures: thick green dandelion stem, natural seed-head platform, woven baskets, translucent white dandelion fluff, tall grass, tree bark, leaves. Surreal scale but physically believable. Warm golden-hour light, volumetric sunlight, realistic shadows, shallow depth of field when close, epic wide scale when pulled back.\n\nCAMERA:\nSmooth cinematic camera only. No abrupt cuts. No sudden object popping. No sudden change of basket count. Start close on boarding, reveal the enormous tree-sized dandelion, show the same visible baskets detaching, then follow the main character's basket in flight.\n\nNEGATIVE / MUST NOT:\nNo single basket under the whole dandelion.\nNo hot-air-balloon structure.\nNo small normal-sized dandelion.\nNo sudden appearance of extra baskets.\nNo crowd of hundreds of baskets.\nNo dense unreadable seed cloud.\nNo modern buildings.\nNo city skyline.\nNo text, no captions, no logos.\nDo not change @image1."
